    @* Start Section description*@
    <div class="container-fluid">
        <div class="col-md-3"></div>
        <div class="col-md-6 " style="text-align:justify;font-size:18px;">
            <h1 style="font-weight:bold;font-size:2em">Emergency Ambulance Service</h1>
            <p>In the war-torn country of Afghanistan, where every second counts and lives hang in the balance, Human Relief Mission's emergency ambulance service stands as a beacon of hope. With unwavering dedication and a commitment to saving lives, we have been at the forefront of providing critical medical assistance to those in need. </p>

            @* Start Qoute Section*@
            <div class="" style="padding-bottom:50px;margin-top:30px;">

                <div class="quote-container col-md-12">
                    <span class="" style="font-size:4em;font-weight:bold">&lsquo;&lsquo;</span>
                    <p class="quote">
                        ...whoever saves a life, it will be as if they saved all of humanity
                    </p>
                    <p class="">Quran</p>
                </div>

            </div>
            @* End Qoute Section*@
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
            <p>In a country like Afghanistan which is plagued by conflict and instability, access to immediate medical care is often limited or non-existent. That's where we step in with our fleet of ambulances and trained medical staff. They navigate through treacherous terrains and volatile areas to reach even the most remote corners of Afghanistan.</p>
            <p>From responding to emergencies caused by conflicts and natural disasters to providing essential healthcare services in underserved communities, our ambulances are always on the frontlines of humanitarian aid in Afghanistan.</p>
            <p>
                <img src="~/Content/projects/ambulance-services/1717756431800.jpg" style="width:100%;" />
            </p>
            <p>The impact of Human Relief Mission's emergency ambulance service cannot be overstated. Countless lives have been saved through their swift response times and expert medical care. They are not just providing transportation; they are delivering hope and a chance at survival for those who would otherwise have none.</p>
            <p>But their work goes beyond immediate crisis response. Human Relief Mission also focuses on building sustainable healthcare systems within Afghanistan. They collaborate with local authorities and communities to train healthcare professionals, establish clinics, and improve overall access to quality healthcare services.</p>
            <p>In a world often filled with despair, it is organisations like Human Relief Mission that restore our faith in humanity. Their selfless dedication reminds us that even amidst chaos and adversity, compassion can prevail.</p>
            <p>As we acknowledge the incredible efforts of Human Relief Mission's emergency ambulance service in Afghanistan, let us stand together in support of their mission - a mission rooted in saving lives and bringing hope to a nation in need.</p>
            <p>
                <img src="~/Content/projects/ambulance-services/emergency-ambulance-2.jpg" style="width:100%;" />
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-3"></div>
    </div>
    @* Start Section description*@

    @* Start Section providing bread*@
    <div class="container-fluid">
        <div class="col-md-3"></div>
        <div class="col-md-6 " style="text-align:justify;font-size:18px;">
            <h1 style="font-weight:bold;font-size:2em">
                What Islam say about live saving
            </h1>
            <p>In Islam, saving a life is considered a noble and highly esteemed act. The Quran teaches that saving a single life is akin to saving all of humanity (Quran 5:32).</p>
            <p>The preservation of life is a fundamental principle in Islamic teachings, emphasizing the importance of compassion, mercy, and responsibility towards others.</p>
            <p>Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) also emphasized the significance of saving lives, stating that whoever saves a life, it is as if they have saved all of mankind. This hadith highlights the immense value placed on human life in Islam and encourages believers to prioritize the well-being and safety of others.</p>
            <p>Therefore, in the Islamic faith, efforts to save lives, including through ambulance services and medical interventions, are highly encouraged and considered a virtuous deed. Supporting initiatives that aim to provide emergency medical care and save lives aligns with the teachings of Islam and reflects the core values of compassion and humanity upheld by the religion.</p>

            @* Start Qoute Section 2 *@
            <div class="" style="padding-bottom:50px;margin-top:30px;">

